It might be fun to see it together.

622
43:11.068 --> 43:12.737
- Let's go. - Okay.

623
43:25.082 --> 43:28.127
There's snow falling behind the man's head

624
43:28.961 --> 43:30.963
while there are flowers blooming behind the woman's back.

625
43:31.964 --> 43:33.090
I wonder what it means.

626
43:36.761 --> 43:41.891
Maybe they were in love until winter passed and spring came.

627
43:42.558 --> 43:43.976
That makes sense.

628
43:44.060 --> 43:46.270
Love is like the seasons, after all.

629
43:47.813 --> 43:48.814
What do you think, Dal?

630
43:50.566 --> 43:53.945
The man has his eyes open, while the woman has hers closed.

631
43:54.028 --> 43:56.948
It means he's bored enough to stare blankly into space.

632
43:57.240 --> 43:59.325
And she's lost in her own world without even realizing it.

633
43:59.909 --> 44:02.662
One side is frozen while the other is blooming.

634
44:03.120 --> 44:04.830
I think it represents the state of their hearts.

635
44:05.122 --> 44:06.707
This isn't love.

636
44:06.999 --> 44:08.000
It's a tragedy.

637
44:11.504 --> 44:15.758
Did something happen today to put you in a bad mood?

638
44:16.217 --> 44:18.344
- No. - Yeon-su, just let him be.

639
44:18.427 --> 44:19.845
I shouldn't have asked.

640
44:24.183 --> 44:27.937
How do you manage to be negative

641
44:28.646 --> 44:30.940
about love every time?

642
44:32.775 --> 44:34.610
I'm not being negative. I'm being realistic.

643
44:35.695 --> 44:38.739
The essence of what humans call love

644
44:39.156 --> 44:41.325
is ultimately based on the desire to reproduce.

645
44:42.243 --> 44:45.162
You could say it's a kind of hormonal response

646
44:45.246 --> 44:47.039
from the urge to increase the chances of reproduction.

647
44:47.748 --> 44:49.417
Oh, here we go again.

648
44:49.500 --> 44:51.711
The human brain isn't that romantic.

649
44:54.797 --> 44:56.924
You can become attached to one person

650
44:57.425 --> 44:59.760
and still feel sexual desires for a stranger.

651
45:23.576 --> 45:25.911
ILLUSION SOMETHING YOU CAN'T GRASP OR CONTAIN

652
45:28.748 --> 45:30.333
You don't know what to do either, do you?

653
45:30.750 --> 45:33.419
What to put inside.

654
45:34.879 --> 45:37.965
Whether it's feelings or desire

655
45:38.507 --> 45:40.259
I don't have a clue either.

656
45:45.598 --> 45:47.933
PUT YOUR HAND INSIDE WHAT YOU GRASP IS WHAT YOU DESIRE

657
46:00.321 --> 46:02.823
LOVE IS THEREFORE A RED TRAFFIC LIGHT

658
46:13.209 --> 46:14.668
How about a buy-one-get-one-free event?

659
46:14.752 --> 46:17.088
Buy one men's toy and get a women's toy free.

660
46:17.171 --> 46:19.298
The world isn't made up of just male-female couples.

661
46:19.590 --> 46:22.385
Targeting only certain couples doesn't suit our identity.

662
46:22.468 --> 46:23.803
What do you think, Yeon-su?

663
46:24.512 --> 46:27.348
A flashy event might grab people's attention

664
46:27.431 --> 46:29.517
but marketing needs to capture their hearts.

665
46:30.309 --> 46:31.894
For attention to lead to a purchase

666
46:31.977 --> 46:34.021
we first need to spark curiosity about the product.

667
46:35.356 --> 46:37.608
So I had an idea.

668
46:39.693 --> 46:40.736
Random.

669
46:42.113 --> 46:44.615
- "Random"? - We use the excitement

670
46:44.698 --> 46:46.200
that comes from the unexpected.

671
46:46.283 --> 46:47.827
Like a mystery box.

672
46:47.910 --> 46:49.120
I'm not sure I follow.

673
46:49.412 --> 46:52.915
We pick out products for people who don't know what they should buy.

674
46:52.998 --> 46:55.584
But why would anyone buy something when they don't know what's inside?

675
46:56.043 --> 46:57.336
That's exactly why they buy it.

676
46:57.837 --> 46:59.422
I'd totally want one.

677
46:59.505 --> 47:02.299
Aren't you dying to know what's inside?

678
47:02.383 --> 47:05.386
The concept itself is so sexy.

679
47:05.469 --> 47:08.180
But sex toys are such a matter of personal preference.

680
47:08.264 --> 47:09.807
So we'd need to build a database.

681
47:10.307 --> 47:12.476
Married couples, couples, or singles

682
47:12.560 --> 47:14.854
from their individual preferences to their sexual fantasies.

683
47:15.438 --> 47:16.689
- Right? - Yes.

684
47:16.939 --> 47:18.983
We could also customize the contents based on concepts

685
47:19.066 --> 47:21.652
like sexless couples, couples going through a rough patch

686
47:21.735 --> 47:23.446
or a masturbation kit.

687
47:25.072 --> 47:26.240
Sounds good.

688
47:26.323 --> 47:28.367
It's almost too good to use for just an event.

689
47:28.451 --> 47:29.452
Sounds like fun.

690
47:31.579 --> 47:34.206
But how did you come up with such an idea?

691
47:34.457 --> 47:36.459
At the art museum last time.

692
47:36.709 --> 47:39.336
There was a box in one of the installations.

693
47:39.420 --> 47:43.007
You could randomly pull out a piece of paper with a note on it.

694
47:43.340 --> 47:44.467
I got curious

695
47:44.675 --> 47:48.721
and the message I happened to pick really resonated with me.

696
47:49.221 --> 47:52.308
- That's why. - You can watch the same thing

697
47:52.725 --> 47:54.602
and one person gets bored while another gets inspired.

698
47:55.603 --> 47:56.812
That's why she's a pro.

699
47:57.521 --> 47:58.981
You're a professional for a reason.

700
48:08.491 --> 48:10.743
Then let's go with the random box.

701
48:10.826 --> 48:13.204
- Yes. - All right.

702
48:14.038 --> 48:16.874
How about we discuss the specific products over some beer?

703
48:16.957 --> 48:19.293
- Love it. - Let's go right now. Sounds great.

704
48:19.376 --> 48:21.545
Let's go. Let's wrap things up.

705
48:21.629 --> 48:22.796
I heard that place was really good.

706
48:22.880 --> 48:25.174
That place we went to was so good. Why did it close down?

707
48:25.257 --> 48:27.009
- Where? - You know.

708
48:27.092 --> 48:28.677
- You haven't tried it? - I didn't go with you.

709
48:28.761 --> 48:29.845
It was really good.

710
48:29.929 --> 48:31.055
You're not sulking, are you?

711
48:31.514 --> 48:32.640
Excuse me.

712
48:33.724 --> 48:35.976
I'll head home first.

713
48:36.060 --> 48:38.145
Why? You came all the way here.

714
48:39.104 --> 48:41.398
I'm suddenly not feeling very well.

715
48:41.774 --> 48:43.359
Well, that's a buzzkill.

716
48:43.442 --> 48:45.528
You were supposed to be the star tonight.

717
48:45.611 --> 48:48.489
- I'm sorry. I'll join next... - It can't be helped.

718
48:48.572 --> 48:49.573
Go on, then.

719
48:51.033 --> 48:52.159
Right.

720
48:52.993 --> 48:54.453
Okay, then.

721
48:54.537 --> 48:56.497
Should I take you home?

722
48:56.580 --> 48:57.790
Oh, no.

723
48:58.749 --> 49:00.543
I'll go by myself.

724
49:00.918 --> 49:02.503
Oh, what a shame.

725
49:05.839 --> 49:08.425
Let's go inside and raise a glass to ourselves.

726
49:08.509 --> 49:09.718
- Come on, Mr. Yun. - Let's go!

727
49:09.802 --> 49:12.263
- You should lead the way. - All right. Let's go.

728
49:12.346 --> 49:14.557
- Lead the way. - Hey, let's go.

729
49:18.269 --> 49:20.104
He must've felt uncomfortable too.

730
49:20.396 --> 49:22.731
He brushed me off like he'd been waiting for the chance.

731
49:23.482 --> 49:27.278
Why does he get to do that? I should've been the one to do it.

732
49:33.117 --> 49:34.410
Darn it.

733
50:05.566 --> 50:07.276
You walk fast.

734
50:08.152 --> 50:09.153
What about dinner?

735
50:09.820 --> 50:11.238
It was canceled because of someone.

736
50:13.741 --> 50:15.284
Why don't we find shelter over there?

737
50:44.229 --> 50:46.023
Are you feeling okay?

738
50:49.735 --> 50:52.696
- I'm fine. - Did you review the contract?

739
50:55.240 --> 50:58.744
Are you really bringing up the contract here?

740
51:01.997 --> 51:03.499
Then what am I supposed to talk about?

741
51:06.460 --> 51:07.711
Why did you do it?

742
51:08.837 --> 51:10.089
That day.

743
51:11.674 --> 51:13.342
Why did you kiss me?

744
51:21.058 --> 51:22.559
I just wanted to.

745
51:23.102 --> 51:24.269
With you, Yeon-su.

746
51:25.145 --> 51:26.146
I know...

747
51:27.189 --> 51:29.817
I apologize if it made you feel uncomfortable.

748
51:30.234 --> 51:32.736
...that I shouldn't be doing this with him.

749
51:33.362 --> 51:34.488
However...

750
51:36.615 --> 51:38.409
I'm really sorry

751
51:39.076 --> 51:41.537
but there's something I have to confirm.

752
51:43.455 --> 51:45.416
Please forgive my rudeness.

753
51:45.624 --> 51:47.251
- Sorry? - Then...

754
51:48.127 --> 51:50.421
Excuse me for a moment.

755
52:41.597 --> 52:43.348
CONTRADICTION BY YANG GUI-JA

756
52:43.432 --> 52:45.267
LOVE IS THEREFORE A RED TRAFFIC LIGHT

757
52:45.350 --> 52:47.144
YOU MUST STOP THE MOMENT IT TURNS ON

758
52:47.227 --> 52:48.937
IT WARNS OF DANGER WHILE ALSO SIGNALING SAFETY

759
52:49.021 --> 52:52.691
THAT RED TRAFFIC LIGHT IS LOVE

760
53:20.594 --> 53:23.764
- Oh, no. - Wait...

761
53:25.307 --> 53:27.518
- Ms. Gong? - Mr. Dokgo.

762
53:28.393 --> 53:31.188
Why are you doing this to me?

763
53:32.272 --> 53:33.607
What do you mean?

764
53:33.982 --> 53:35.275
You started it this time.

765
53:36.985 --> 53:38.570
Mr. Dokgo.

766
53:40.155 --> 53:41.990
But you're gay.

767
53:52.543 --> 53:53.544
I'm sorry?

768
53:53.877 --> 53:58.257
And yet, I want to feel every part of this stranger.

769
54:06.390 --> 54:10.352
MAKE ME TINGLE

770
54:26.326 --> 54:28.328
Let's prepare the other ingredients.

771
54:28.871 --> 54:30.789
I like zucchini

772
54:30.873 --> 54:33.709
so I'll dice up about a quarter of one.

773
54:34.543 --> 54:38.046
Chop the onion and green onion and set them aside.

774
54:38.672 --> 54:40.257
When making the broth

775
54:40.340 --> 54:43.552
don't boil the anchovies for too long or the broth turns bitter.

776
54:43.635 --> 54:45.262
That's odd. The gas won't turn on.

777
54:45.345 --> 54:47.347
Why are you suddenly cooking?

778
54:47.431 --> 54:48.974
- I just... - Just order food.

779
54:49.516 --> 54:50.976
So how do I turn this thing on?

780
54:51.310 --> 54:53.270
- Did you open the gas valve? - Valve?
